    <TIER LINGUISTIC_TYPE_REF="default-lt" TIER_ID="default"/>
    <TIER LINGUISTIC_TYPE_REF="imported-sep" TIER_ID="SPEAKER_00">
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a1"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts4" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts51">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>A well-known and respected tech CEO Dario Amodei, who heads a cutting-edge AI company called Anthropic, is raising alarms tonight about AI's potential impact on employment that could soon be felt. While he says AI can lead to incredible advancements like medical breakthroughs and boost the economy, he believes it could also lead to half of entry-level white-collar jobs disappearing and 10 to 20% unemployment in the next one to five years. It's something that's been talked about within tech circles for a while, but rarely so starkly and so publicly. I spoke to him just before AIR about that and other implications he thinks AI may have on society.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a2"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts55" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts71">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Dario, you've said that AI could wipe out half of all entry-level white-collar jobs and spike unemployment to 10 to 20%, how soon might that happen?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a8"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts191" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts246">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>You are running an incredibly important company in AI, and you know this better than anybody, or as well as all the names we know, people, Sam Altman and others who are working, Elon Musk in AI. Why are you raising the alarm? Because it's not necessarily, I would think, in your best interest. Because a lot of the messages we hear from, at least publicly from some AI CEOs and stuff, is a little bit more calming, like, you know, these agents are going to be great in your life, and yes, there may be problems, but writ large, this is a fantastic thing.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a14"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts343" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts416">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I do want to read something that Sam Altman, your former boss at OpenAI said in September. He was saying that AI can cause significant, in his words, significant change in labor markets, good and bad. He went on to say that most jobs will change more slowly than most people think. And then he said this, and I want to just read a word for word. He said: "many of the jobs we do today would have looked like trifling waste of time to people a few hundred years ago, but nobody is looking back at the past. Wishing they were a lamplighter. If a lamplighter could see the world today, he would think the prosperity all around him was unimaginable. And if we could fast forward a hundred years from today, the prosperity all around us would feel just as unimaginable."</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a18"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts418" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts436">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>For younger people, I should say lamplighters was actually a job. People went around, lighting lamps on the streets. I think a lot of people may not even know what a lamp lighter is. But do you think Sam Altman is wrong?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a20"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts479" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts500">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Well, let me just say because you've previously in the past said you've described a future where cancer is cured, the economy grows at 10% a year, the budget is balanced, and 20% of people don't have jobs.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a22"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts599" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts633">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Do we as a society even understand the potential inequalities that this may amplify? And also the impact just on what, like I have little kids, I have a five-year-old and a three-year-old. What do they grow up aspiring to if machines can do pretty much everything better? What does it do to initiative or drive or striving? And I don't know the answer to that, but it it concerns me.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a25"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts695" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts737">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>During testing your company's latest chatbot, Claude Four, was capable of what was described as extreme blackmail. Specifically, I understand it threatened to reveal an engineer's extramarital affair when it was told it would be taken offline and replaced. This was a simulation. Were you surprised by that? And what is that? I mean, that freaked me out when I read that. What does that mean?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a591"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts801" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts803">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>[inaudible]</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a30"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts845" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts863">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I mean does it uh the obvious question is does that pretend AI becoming self-aware and which could and could that lead to dire consequences.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a35"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts919" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts925">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>What are practical steps?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a37"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts949" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts954">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Logically lawmakers I guess, really.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a43"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts1080" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts1085">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Dario, thank you so much. It's really fascinating.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
    </TIER>
